<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="stachyose degradation" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-6527" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Arabidopsis thaliana col&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Accept-If-Predicted Pathways (AIPP) generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are present widely throughout the plant kingdom. The AIPP list contains pathways that are automatically accepted if they are predicted for any plant species database. However, AIPP pathways are not automatically imported into databases if they are not predicted by the Pathologic program. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; Translocation of |FRAME: CPD-1099| and |FRAME: CPD-170| is pronounced in members of the |FRAME: TAX-3650| family. One of the photosynthetic products in |FRAME: TAX-3650| is translocated as |FRAME: CPD-1099| and |FRAME: CPD-170| |CITS: [12943544]|. Galactose metabolism in fruits is poorly understood as compared to sucrose metabolism, |FRAME: TAX-3650| plants are excellent models to elucidate the various pathways of galactose metabolism, particularly those involved in fruit ripening |CITS: [16829585]|. This pathway describes the degradation of |FRAME: CPD-170| and |FRAME: CPD-1099| and recruitment of |FRAME: ALPHA-D-GALACTOSE| into the fruit sink where a series of enzymes phosphorylate them. Free galactose is not present in the sink tissues. The |FRAME: CPD-1099| and |FRAME: CPD-170| oligosaccharides are first subjected to &amp;alpha;-galactosidase activity, which release free galactose into the sink tissue. The pathway begins by the hydrolytic removal of |FRAME: ALPHA-D-GALACTOSE| and is translocated into the fruit sink |CITS: [16662141]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="PMN" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
    <Author name="O-28" />
    <Author name="pujar" />
  </Authors>
