    <DataNode elementId="AT3G06580-MONOMER" textLabel="galactokinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SEE5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Galactokinase is the first committed enzyme of the Leloir pathway of &lt;i&gt;D&lt;/i&gt;-galactose metabolism (|FRAME:GALACTMETAB-PWY|). It allows the conversion of galactose into galactose-1-phosphate. Galactose-1-phosphate is known to be interfere with the metabolism of &lt;i&gt;D&lt;/i&gt;-hexoses and is a possible cause of galactose toxicity in plants; it has therefore been proposed that galactokinase plays an important role in the regulation of hexose metabolism. The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana AGK1&lt;/i&gt; gene was shown to complement a &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; &amp;Delta;&lt;i&gt;gal1&lt;/i&gt; galactokinase mutant |CITS:[9225860]| and its direct activit has been demonstrated &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [19509290]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G06580-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G06580.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9SEE5" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Swissmodel" value="Q9SEE5" />
