    <DataNode elementId="AT2G35020-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64765" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">UDP-N-acetylglucosamine (UDP-GlcNAc) is an essential precursor for glycoprotein and glycolipid biosynthesis in plants and it can also serve as a regulatory modification on signaling proteins. This enzyme, GlcNAc1pUT2, is capable of synthesizing |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE| (UDP-GlcNAc) from |FRAME: UTP| and |FRAME: N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE-1-P| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [20557289]|. It can also catalyze the reverse reaction using |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-GlcNAc| and the less common 4-epimer, |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-GALACTOSAMINE| (UDP-GalNAc) |CITS: [20557289]|. In addition, unlike the related protein |FRAME: AT1G31070-MONOMER GlcNAc1pUT1|, this enzyme can also act on |FRAME: GLC-1-P|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G35020-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G35020.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11952" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF01704" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR029044" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="UDP-N-acetylgalactosamine diphosphorylase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="UTP--glucose-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
